Those are DexHand descriptions from https://github.com/iotdesignshop, vendored
so the arm models build, plus one directory of meshes mirrored from them. Each
directory keeps its upstream LICENSE and a VENDORED.md recording the exact
commit it came from.

CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 is **NonCommercial** and **ShareAlike**: it forbids commercial
use, and derivative works must carry the same licence. That is why the mirrored
left-hand meshes are marked CC BY-NC-SA rather than MIT — reflecting a mesh
produces a derivative of it. The generated URDFs that reference those meshes and
embed DexHand joint values should be treated the same way.

Full detail, including which generated files are affected and how to obtain a
tree with no CC BY-NC-SA content in it, is in:

    ros2_ws/THIRD_PARTY.md

